{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/610599-activating-a-gift-1-action","id":610599,"title":"Activating a Gift = 1 Action?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-08-01T02:55:19-07:00","id":610599,"title":"Activating a Gift = 1 Action?","content":"Hello, it may seems a stupid question but I can't find anything in the corebook that tells me what kind of action activating a gift is.<br /> <br /> In some gifts (like Razor Claws) it's said that the gift takes &quot;1 full round to sharp the claws&quot;, but what's the general rule? If, let's say, I want to use Lambent Flame do I have to spend 1 action?<br /> <br /> My first storyteller told me that activating any gift is a reflexive action, unless otherwise stated, but this seems overpowered, especially with higher rank gifts in which I could do tons of damages and then still attack at full rage.<br /> <br /> How do you handle this? Is there any reference on the core 20th anniversary book that I am missing?<br /> <br /> Thanks<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5825-werepanda","name":"Werepanda","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5825_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T02:58:31-07:00","id":610615,"title":"","content":"Unless the gift is obviously part of another action, I rule that it's an action of its own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3118-cifer","name":"Cifer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3118_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T03:09:50-07:00","id":610621,"title":"","content":"And in this case how do you handle multiple actions?<br /> <br /> If a gifts requires a roll I can imagine you would handle it like any other roll, by splitting the dice pool between the gift activation roll and the roll of the other action (let's say a bite). But what about gifts that don't require any roll (like Lambent Flame)? Do you allow players to split their actions? If so, given that there's no &quot;dice pool&quot; for the activation of the gift, what kind of penalty do you give for the additional action?<br /> <br /> Last question: what's the difference between gifts that say &quot;1 full round&quot; and a normal gift then?<br /> <br /> Thanks and sorry if I overwhelmed you with all these questions :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5825-werepanda","name":"Werepanda","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5825_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T03:21:25-07:00","id":610625,"title":"","content":"Firstly, I use Revised rules for dice-splitting (first action subtracts [total number of actions] dice, every further action subtracts one more), meaning that even if a gift has no activation roll, it will at least make the other actions more difficult unless the entire turn consists of diceless actions.<br /> As for the full round: It takes exactly that, one full round, with no possibility for action-splitting or rage expenditure for more actions. Personally, I'm not quite sure how they figured this would balance out (Razor Claws already took the full turn in previous editions when it was pathetically weak), but that's how I play it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3118-cifer","name":"Cifer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3118_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T03:26:09-07:00","id":610626,"title":"","content":"Thanks for your clarifications! Usually I use the 20th edition rules for multiple actions, but maybe I could use the revised rules just to cover this peculiar cases of non-roll Gifts. It should work, thanks again <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5825-werepanda","name":"Werepanda","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5825_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T11:01:34-07:00","id":611081,"title":"","content":"The &quot;standard rule&quot; is that anything that is not <i>specifically</i> a reflexive action is a standard action, and thus &quot;uses an action.&quot;<br /> <br /> Reflexive actions are as follows:<br /> - Yielding your initiative position.<br /> - Spending Rage<br /> - healing damage<br /> - soaking damage<br /> - reverting to breed form<br /> - speaking<br /> <br /> There are a few limits there; &quot;speaking&quot; does not include <i>oration</i> or other speech-derived actions (lying to the mall cop is an action, not a reflexive action - even if lying to mall cops is a reflex for you as it is for me!) Rage has internal limits to how much can be spent in a turn. With the exception of soaking damage, you have to be conscious for this stuff, too. There are also other things that are &quot;reflexive&quot; but aren't actually <i>actions</i>, like rolling for Frenzy or making a Willpower check to resist something.<br /> <br /> However, each Gift is unique, and as far as actions are concerned, there are numerous types.<br /> <br /> - Automatic Gifts. These are Gifts that have a permanent effect once learned, like Spirit of the Fray or Balance. it also includes &quot;at will&quot; gifts like Scent of Sight, Resist Toxin, or Call the Breeze<br /> - <i>Clearly</i> Reflexive Gifts. These specifically use reflexive actions to function. Hare's Leap, Flame Dance, and Lightning Reflexes are the only core book Gifts that are <i>specifically</i> reflexive.<br /> - <i>Apparently</i> Reflexive Gifts: These use reflexive mechanics and &quot;feel&quot; Reflexive, but are not <i>specified</i> to be Reflexive. City Running, for example.<br /> - Standard action Gifts: Pretty much the majority of Gifts.<br /> - Full-turn Gifts: These specify that they take a full turn to enact, and so can be your only action (besides reflexives.) Razor Claws is the most famous example.<br /> - Multiple-turn Gifts: These are Gifts that require extended rolls. The only one I noticed in the core Book is Roll Over, but I've seen them elsewhere.<br /> - Mini-Rituals: The activation of these Gifts is measured in minutes, rather than actions or turns. Song of the Earth Mother and Inner Strength.<br /> \u200b- Action modifier Gifts: <i>These</i> are the weird ones. Things like Black Mark, Falling Touch, and Liar's Face. These say &quot;When you do X, you can use this Gift as well.&quot; it's not clear if you're using them reflexively, or if you are splitting a standard action; some require rolls, others do not, but they all <i>clearly</i> take place at the same time as the action you are modifying with them.<br /> <br /> I usually err on the side of power in RPG's - more powerful characters are generally more fun for players, and it gives me license to make more powerful dangers for them to face in turn. So I would rule that the last category are in fact reflexive actions that are <i>reliant</i> on succeeding the action they modify (Rattler's Bite doesn't work if you don't actually succeed your bite, and Liar's Face won't work if you botch your attempt to tell the truth - it can happen!)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":612,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/612-the-cat-came-back","user":"The Cat Came Back","date":". 08-01-2015, 02:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/612-the-cat-came-back","name":"The Cat Came Back","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar612_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"243"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T11:34:08-07:00","id":611103,"title":"","content":"This covers pretty much the entire spectrum.<br /> <br /> Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5825-werepanda","name":"Werepanda","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5825_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-05T00:43:08-07:00","id":616063,"title":"","content":"I've always interpreted gifts without activation rolls or which do not specify their own duration do not really count as an action.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}